WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.679
When the answer lives in release notes,

2
00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:05.600
you can bring the source
into the session as text.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.592
Web fetch reads this sample GitHub
release and returns its notes.

4
00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:15.720
The agent uses the text to find
which command line flag changed.

5
00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.165
Keep the source handy
when you use the answer.

6
00:00:30.165 --> 00:00:33.587
It gives you somewhere to check
what the release actually says.
